   30                                   ;                   Fig 1. Ascii rendering of the 'kiss of death' web.
   31                                   ;                                                                                                                 
   32                                   ; This source code was originally 'leaked' by 'JaySmith2000' in August 2008,
   33                                   ; who sold it on CD as part of a release entitled the 'Jaguar Sector II Source Code
   34                                   ; Collection':
   35                                   ;     https://web.archive.org/web/20131117222232/http://www.jaysmith2000.com/Jagpriceguide.htm
   36                                   ;
   37                                   ; This is a cleaned-up and commented version of the source code file 'antelope.gas'.
   38                                   ;
   39                                   ; No code has been changed, so this source file can be used to create a build
   40                                   ; of Tempest 2000 that is byte-for-byte identical to the original 1994 release.
   41                                   ;
   42                                   ; All original variable and routine names are preserved. The changes include:
   43                                   ;   - Fixed up indentation.
   44                                   ;   - Added comments and routine headers.
   45                                   ;
   46                                   ; The home of this file and the rest of the Tempest 2000 source code is:
   47                                   ;     https://github.com/mwenge/tempest2k 
   48                                   ;
   49                                   ; antelope.gas contains the following routines:
   50                                   ; Mode 1 = poly
   51                                   ; Mode 2 = pretty_poly
   52                                   ; Mode 3 = tile16
   53                                   ; Mode 4 = rex
   54                                   ; Mode 5 = snglpix
   55                                   ; Mode 6 = pring
   56                                   ; Mode 7 = pring2


